{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210734,"nonce":"Bcmcx1adAJpPfdavkZ9RJIU463Y=","title":"Plugins migrated to wlift_abi opaque-VM C shim","message":"Fixed; see git log for the landing commit. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n\nThe plugin-ABI work shipped across phases A–E (commits 5ac41ce → 8ecdfbb plus the cleanup pass). Native plugin cdylibs (`@hatch:sqlite`, `@hatch:gpu`, `@hatch:image`, `@hatch:audio`, `@hatch:physics`, `@hatch:window`) now depend only on `crates/wlift_abi` — a header-only crate that declares `Value`, `ObjType`, `TypedArrayKind`, an opaque `WrenVm`, and `extern \"C\"` decls for the ~22 host entry points the plugins actually need.\n\nHost process exports `#[no_mangle] wlift_plugin_*` symbols from `src/plugin_abi.rs`; the dynamic linker resolves a plugin's externs against them at `dlopen` (with `-Wl,-undefined,dynamic_lookup` on macOS / `--unresolved-symbols=ignore-in-object-files` on Linux, emitted by each plugin's `build.rs`). The wasm static-link path resolves the same `extern \"C\"` decls against `wren_lift`'s exports at link time — single shim, two link strategies.\n\nVM/GcImpl/ObjList layout changes in `wren_lift` can't reach plugin code anymore. The `wlift_plugin_abi_version` handshake is kept at 1 because the new exports are additive; bump it on any wire-shape change (Value bit layout, ObjType discriminant renumbering, function signature change, function removal).\n\nVerified end-to-end: hatch.wrenlift.com boots clean under both `hatch run hatch/site` (tiered) and `wlift --aot hatch/site/site_aot` with all sqlite symbols resolving, catalog hydrating to 40 packages, `/readyz=200`.\n\n---\n\n\nWhen a `wlift_*` plugin cdylib depended on `wren_lift = { ..., default-features = false }` (no `host`) while the host binary built with `default = host + cranelift`, Cargo compiled **two** rlibs of `wren_lift` — one with `host`, one without. `VM` has at least one host-gated field (`native_temp_dirs: Vec\u003cTempDir\u003e` at the time of writing), so layouts diverged. The plugin's `\u0026mut VM` decode read at the wrong offset, and the first foreign-method dispatch silently SIGSEGV'd (rc=139, no diagnostic).\n\nThe runtime ABI handshake (commit c22768c, `wlift_plugin_abi_version()` → `WLIFT_PLUGIN_ABI_VERSION`) did **not** catch this — it only flagged version-number drift, not feature-set drift.\n\n**Why it bit:** Hatch CI run 25059733493 (2026-04-28) exited with 139 on hatch-image / hatch-physics / hatch-sqlite right at the first plugin call. Then again 2026-05-28: site under AOT SIGSEGV'd in `Catalog.boot` until we rebuilt the sqlite dylib against current `wren_lift` and went on workspace path-deps in `hatch/site/hatchfile`.\n\n**How to apply (post-resolution):** New plugins use `wlift_abi = { path = \"../../crates/wlift_abi\" }` as their only wren_lift-adjacent dep. No `host` feature, no `wren_lift` import. Copy `plugins/wlift_sqlite/build.rs` for the platform link flags.","files":null}]}